  "description": "Addition of an open oak framed porch to the front door area of the property. The existing porch was unsafe as it had been built with no foundations and was falling over (75mm lower on the left side) and needed to be demolished before it collapsed.\nThe new porch that has been built has been designed by the carpenter to compliment the existing Mock Tudor appearance of the property, utilising solid oak beams where appropriate and clay tiles to match those on the existing roof.\nThe porch has been built to a greater height than 'usual' in order to preserve and display the original brick and tile projection above the doorway (image attached) that had been obscured by the previous porch addition (which was not original to the property as built in 1926).  As an original feature it was felt this should be retained and restored (it has been re-pointed) and not removed or damaged in order to accommodate a lower ridge line of the porch roof.",
